      "text": "To solve \\(\\left\\lceil -\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} \\right\\rceil\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Evaluate the expression inside the square root:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{49}{4}\n   \\]\n   This can be rewritten as:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{49}{4} = 12.25\n   \\]\n\n2. **Take the square root of 12.25:**\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{12.25} = 3.5\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the negative of the square root:**\n   \\[\n   -\\sqrt{12.25} = -3.5\n   \\]\n\n4. **Apply the ceiling function:**\n   The ceiling function \\(\\left\\lceil x \\right\\rceil\\) returns the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(x\\). For \\(x = -3.5\\), the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(-3.5\\) is \\(-3\\).\n\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil -3.5 \\right\\rceil = -3\n   \\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
